+# Earlier profiles: shared reading preferences
+
+Earlier profiles uses the game's existing Theme/Plain text, Standard/Large text size and effective Reduced effects settings. The lightweight display entry starts before Recovery loads version/catalog information, so loading and failure explanations use the same reading policy. This page has no preference-writing controls: change display settings in the game's Options and return.
+
+Only host text and effect attributes change. Existing Find, Review, Cancel, Back and explicit file-download actions retain their owners. Reading settings do not inspect additional profiles, replace an original choice, cancel an active read, reverify files, clear a prepared link or take focus. System reduction combines with the saved setting. A denied storage read uses defaults plus the available system signal and makes no attempt to save.
+
+The existing Recovery lifecycle still closes/cancels data work on pagehide and restarts discovery setup on a persisted return. The display owner survives persisted departure and rereads current shared/system settings; terminal departure disposes it. This does **not** promise that an earlier selected profile or prepared link survives a full Recovery return. No profile migration, repair, restore, writer permission or backup scope is added.
+
+The page reuses packaged Field Kit fonts, semantic text sizes, square controls and the keyboard/controller focus treatment. All new runtime dependencies are already under the existing `game` distribution include. No authoring-only helper, external font service, new art or build/version change is required.
+
+## Candidate verification boundary
+
+This proposal is based on exact source `a13ab970222498d7c5fa7f62f9fc04fe436979d5`, tree `cf744b1ced9680b2fb4e0c304ddfc4b9f44b3e86`; it is not yet integrated or released. The five complete affected files pass **68/68** on Node 20.19.5 and **68/68** on Node 22.22.2. The unchanged original page fails all five new display cases. The bounded fixture has 94 explicit source inputs / 1,125,433 bytes and remains identical throughout both candidate runs. Syntax and changed-file formatting checks pass.
+
+The new cases load the actual markup-selected display/application entries, hold release-information loading, retain the original failure explanation and Back action, model an unavailable application graph, deny display storage, and exercise selected-original/pending-read/prepared-download/focus preservation through the actual Recovery view with an injected read-only reader. Those small Blob handles test ownership, not image decoding or original-byte integrity. Existing complete recovery-view and selected-original tests retain their separate coverage.
+
+A browser still needs to verify Theme/Plain and Standard/Large at 390×844, 844×390 and desktop, focus-ring clearance, 200% zoom and real system reduction. Navigate through Find/Review and one explicit download using keyboard and a physical controller where available; touch targets require actual touch checks. Record actual display and data state before/after returning from Options. This modeled source result is not native layout, BFCache admission, hardware, public-release or full P03/P05 acceptance.
+
+## Maintainer example
+
+“Open Earlier profiles with saved Plain/Large and system Reduced effects. Hold release information and confirm loading remains readable; then fail it and use Back. In a ready session, select an original, begin verification and change the shared reading setting without disturbing Cancel focus or the pending read. Prepare its exact file, keep the visible download focused, and change reading settings again; the same prepared link must remain. Test cached and terminal display lifecycles separately from Recovery's existing read cancellation. Never add a preference write, new recovery reader or automatic reinspection to solve presentation.”
